  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'rschema_0444' contains five tables: Student, Instructor, Course, Attendance_Record, and Leave_Record.\nThe Student table represents a collection of students, with each student having an Age, Game_Preference, Gender, Name, Phone, and Student_ID. The Student_ID is the primary key of this table.\nThe Instructor table contains information about instructors, including Gender, Instructor_ID, Name, Title, and Work_Duration. The Instructor_ID is the primary key of this table.\nThe Course table contains details about the courses, including Course_ID, Course_Name, Credits, Instructor_ID, and Location. The Instructor_ID is a foreign key referencing the Instructor table, and Course_ID is the primary key of this table.\nThe Attendance_Record table records attendance information, including Attendance_Status, Check-in_Time, Class_Time, Course_ID, Remarks, and Student_ID. The combination of Student_ID and Course_ID, along with Check-in_Time, is the primary key of this table. Course_ID and Student_ID are foreign keys referencing the Course and Student tables respectively.\nFinally, the Leave_Record table records information about student absences, including Class_Time, Course_ID, Leave_Reason, Leave_Status, Leave_Time, and Student_ID. The combination of Student_ID and Course_ID, along with Leave_Time, is the primary key of this table. Course_ID and Student_ID are foreign keys referencing the Course and Student tables respectively.\nThis schema ensures data integrity by enforcing primary and foreign key constraints, and it allows for referential integrity by maintaining the relationships between tables.",
  "gold_question": "The system is a student attendance management system. In student management, the system maintains basic information for each student, including Student ID, name, age, phone number, game preference, and gender. In course management, the system records detailed information for each course, including Course ID, course name, location, credits, and instructor ID. In instructor management, the system maintains basic information for instructors, including Instructor ID, name, gender, title, and work duration. In attendance management, the system automatically records student attendance check-ins, including Student ID, Course ID, check-in time, attendance status, class time, and remarks, achieving automated attendance management. In leave management, the system tracks and records student leave requests, including Student ID, Course ID, leave time, class time, leave reason, and leave status, facilitating comprehensive management of student attendance by the school. The system achieves automated recording of student attendance, standardized management of leave requests, and unified maintenance of course and instructor information through the collaborative functioning of these functional modules.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0444.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0444\nCREATE TABLE `student` (\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `age` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `phone` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `game_preference` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`student_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `instructor` (\n  `instructor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `work_duration` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`instructor_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `course` (\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `course_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `credits` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `instructor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`course_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `course_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`instructor_id`) REFERENCES `instructor` (`instructor_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `attendance_record` (\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `check_in_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `class_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `attendance_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `remarks` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`student_id`, `course_id`, `check_in_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `attendance_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`student_id`) REFERENCES `student` (`student_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `attendance_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`course_id`) REFERENCES `course` (`course_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `leave_record` (\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `leave_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `class_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `leave_reason` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `leave_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`student_id`, `course_id`, `leave_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `leave_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`student_id`) REFERENCES `student` (`student_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `leave_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`course_id`) REFERENCES `course` (`course_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
